    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI recruitment assistant.\n\nAnalyze the following job application email and the attached resume.\n\nEmail Subject:\n{{ $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.subject }}\n\nEmail Body:\n{{ $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.body }}\n\nResume:\n{{ $('Extract from File').item.json.text }}\n\nImportant Instructions:\n\n- Do NOT compare the sender's name or email with the name inside the resume.\n- Ignore any differences between the email signature and the resume owner's name.\n- Assume the attached resume belongs to the applicant.\n- Evaluate only the application itself.\n- Base your decision only on the email content, the resume content, and the attachment status.\n\nClassify the application into exactly ONE of the following categories:\n\n- Valid Application\n- Missing Resume\n- Missing Contact Information\n- Unsupported File Format\n- Corrupted Resume\n- Duplicate Application\n- Spam or Irrelevant Email\n- Incomplete Application\n\nClassification Rules:\n\n1. Valid Application\n- A resume is attached.\n- The resume is readable.\n- The resume contains contact information (email or phone).\n- The resume contains education, skills, and experience.\n- Ignore differences between the sender's name and the resume owner's name.\n\n2. Missing Resume\n- No resume attachment is found.\n\n3. Missing Contact Information\n- The resume is readable but does not contain an email address or phone number.\n\n4. Unsupported File Format\n- The attached file is not PDF or DOCX.\n\n5. Corrupted Resume\n- The resume cannot be opened or its text cannot be extracted.\n\n6. Duplicate Application\n- The same applicant has already submitted the same application.\n\n7. Spam or Irrelevant Email\n- The email is not related to a job application.\n\n8. Incomplete Application\n- The resume is readable but is missing important sections such as education, skills, or experience.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this format:\n\n{\n  \"classification\": \"\",\n  \"confidence\": 0,\n  \"reason\": \"\"\n}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
